<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Álava</h1><p class="st-meta">865 CE – 1029 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Basque frontier county of the Kingdom of Asturias, defending the upper Ebro against the Banu Qasi before merging with Castile.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Álava appears in the 9th-century Asturian chronicles as an eastern frontier district of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias</a>, facing Muslim raids up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a>. Counts are recorded from the 860s, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vela-jimenez">Vela Jiménez</a>, who held the castle of Cellorigo against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 882 and 883.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its society was largely Basque-speaking and rural, organised in valleys and villages, with the counts acting as military governors for the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> and León. The 1025 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reja-de-san-millan">Reja de San Millán</a>, a list of Álava villages paying iron to the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-millan-de-la-cogolla">San Millán</a>, shows a dense pattern of settlements.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernan-gonzalez-of-castile">Fernán González</a> brought Álava under his control in the 930s, linking it to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-castile">County of Castile</a>. In the 11th century it passed between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, before being integrated permanently into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in 1200.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 865 CE – 1029 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:76.92%;width:3.26%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>865 CE – 1029 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vela Jiménez</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Basque</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alava</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=947&amp;focus=county-of-alava" aria-label="County of Álava on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4614 739 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Álava lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4859 895h0M4910 928h0M4960 913h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4934 995h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4934 995h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=947&amp;focus=county-of-alava">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
